  "frontier_coordinate": "R-127 resolves the abstract causal source geometry left by R-126: on each fixed temporally faithful chart the legal adjoint is blockwise E[S_b^*G|F_(t_(b-1))], its physical quotient Riesz vector is sum_b S_b E[S_b^*G|F_(t_(b-1))], and the q=10/9 source completion costs exactly 5/9 of the legal force square. A two-block fixture prevents collapse to unrestricted C_JG. Weighted triangular Schur improves the conditional mixed and far aggregation constants to sqrt(8/7) and sqrt(224/223), but does not prove the production block prototypes; same-channel blocks still add by triangle. The augmented low/injected Loewner theorem shows that saturation leaves room only for b sqrt(zeta)+c sqrt(eta)=0, so a production proof needs this cancellation, a strict matrix margin, or a constant low payment. A constant-gauge no-go requires an absolute low/injected anchor, and coherent residual interpolation exposes the live integrated variance-minus-curvature target with that anchor retained. The live successor is the common identity P_pred L_pi^*D(complete R-093 endpoint action)=g_low/inj^adm+sum_(r,m)g_(r,m)^adm, with every DeltaC/DeltaGamma, heat, cluster, R-063 forest, rational, 2680/729 Cartan, trace, covariance, low, injected, and mean owner present once and invariant under refinement. R-126, R-125, R-121, R-120, R-118, R-103 REG, and R-087/R-093 CORE retain their owners. OVERLAP_src, Nelson, removals, interacting measure, and Sector A remain open.",
